  <h2>Frank Baumholtz (1918&ndash;1997)</h2>
  <p>
    Frank Baumholtz was a Major League Baseball outfielder born in Midvale.
    He played eleven seasons in the majors between 1947 and 1957 for the
    Cincinnati Reds, Chicago Cubs, and Philadelphia Phillies, finishing with a
    career batting average of .290.
  </p>
  <p>
    Baumholtz was also a two-sport college athlete at Ohio University and
    briefly played professional basketball for the Youngstown Bears and the
    Cleveland Rebels of the Basketball Association of America (a precursor to
    the NBA) before settling on baseball as his career.
  </p>
